Origin of the code
------------------
- HeliBoard v4.2 (git tag v4.2, commit 0c60dffb03a4e2e7a37cb82210f5299f93c03979),
  https://github.com/HeliBorg/HeliBoard, GPL-3.0-only. This repository starts from a source import; the upstream history is
  in the HeliBoard repository.
- OpenBoard (https://github.com/openboard-team/openboard), GPL-3.0, from which HeliBoard is forked.
- Android Open Source Project (AOSP) LatinIME keyboard, Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE-Apache-2.0).
  Files derived from AOSP keep their "Copyright (C) The Android Open Source Project" headers and
  their "Apache-2.0 AND GPL-3.0-only" SPDX tags.
- Some layout and keyboard-parser code in HeliBoard is adapted from FlorisBoard
  (https://github.com/florisboard/florisboard, Apache License 2.0). Its headers are kept.
- Glide (gesture) typing: the engine in app/src/main/java/helium314/keyboard/latin/gesture (GlideEngine.kt) is a
  rewrite of FlorisBoard's "statistical glide typing classifier" (StatisticalGlideTypingClassifier.kt) at tag v0.4.0,
  commit 80fb20885ba335947b6fd8f3449de8be11c0e13d (2024-09-18), https://github.com/florisboard/florisboard, Apache License
  2.0 (licence verified in that commit: LICENSE and README), Copyright 2020-2024 Patrick Goldinger and the FlorisBoard
  Contributors. FlorisBoard's class follows Etienne Desticourt's write-up for AnySoftKeyboard
  (https://github.com/AnySoftKeyboard/AnySoftKeyboard/pull/1870, Apache License 2.0, SPDX verified from the repository).
  Kept from them: the model (ideal gesture over the key centres, shape and location distance, Gaussian probabilities, pruning
  by first and last key and by path length) and the constants (standard deviations 22.08 and 0.5109, loop for double
  letters). New in Taen: the code (no Android types), log-domain costs, a dictionary-probability cost term, coarse-then-fine
  scoring, key mapping by base letter for Bulgarian and accented letters, and the word list read from the bundled main
  dictionary. The source files carry "Apache-2.0 AND GPL-3.0-only". CleverKeys (GPL-3.0, tribixbite/CleverKeys at
  96cd1917) was evaluated and not used: its decoders need the prebuilt ONNX Runtime native library and model files, and its
  Bulgarian model is a downloadable pack.

Not included
------------
- The HeliBoard name and launcher icon (CC BY-SA 4.0) are not used. Taen has its own name and a
  placeholder icon.
- HeliBoard's gesture data gathering, its support for loading a user-supplied native library and its
  support for the closed-source Google glide typing library were removed. Glide typing is the open-source
  engine named above; no native library, no model file and no download are involved.

