Voice typing: speech is recognised on the phone, nothing is sent anywhere
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- ONNX Runtime 1.27.0 (com.microsoft.onnxruntime:onnxruntime-android, https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime), MIT License, Copyright (c)
  Microsoft Corporation (licence from the project's GitHub licence file and the POM; checked 2026-11-12). Prebuilt libonnxruntime.so and
  libonnxruntime4j_jni.so for arm64-v8a, taken from Maven Central and pinned by SHA-256 in gradle/verification-metadata.xml (AAR 077dec5e...);
  both are on privacy/native-libs.allow. CPU provider only. Version choice: the AARs of 1.22.0, 1.24.3 and 1.27.0 declare no permission and no
  network class; 1.30.0 and 1.31.1 add the INTERNET permission, a telemetry provider and an HTTP client (read from their manifests and
  class lists), so they are not used. libonnxruntime.so links liblog (its logger); the app sets its log level to fatal and the device audit
  reads logcat.
- Model: NVIDIA parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3 (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3), CC BY 4.0 (the licence field of the model repository), Copyright
  NVIDIA Corporation. The ONNX int8 export used here was made by the sherpa-onnx project (k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx, Apache-2.0) and is published as
  csukuangfj/sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-int8 (also CC BY 4.0), revision ed5d745623472f97cfc2e6c2916ee248798fc5a8. Changes by the
  exporter: conversion to ONNX and quantisation to int8; none by Taen. The model is NOT in the APK and is never downloaded by the app: the builder
  fetches it with `make fetch-voice-model` (tools/voice-model.lock lists URL, size and SHA-256), the user installs the four files or, since 1.0.2, the one
  archive of the same model (the official k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx release asset sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-int8.tar.bz2, 487211443 bytes, SHA-256
  1495e91b59d7fc53ddca91f3431758ec99f8fa253fdb0e1e851be0f72b14b0f9, tools/voice-model-archive.lock; the four files in it were measured equal to the Hugging Face
  files, so the same licence and credit apply), and the app checks the archive and each file's SHA-256 before it is used. The archive is unpacked by the app's
  own bzip2 decoder (Bzip2InputStream.kt, written from the public format description, tested against libbz2 output): no compression library and no new
  dependency was added in 1.0.2. Credit shown to the user in Settings > Voice typing.
- Code: the log-mel front end (Fbank.kt) and the token-and-duration greedy search (TdtGreedy.kt) are new Kotlin written from the published behaviour of
  the model (NeMo preprocessor settings in the model metadata, the sherpa-onnx NeMo transducer decoder). Their oracle, tools/voice/parakeet_ref.py (numpy
  and onnxruntime), and the sherpa-onnx Python package (Apache-2.0) used for the comparison run on the build machine only and are not shipped.
- Test audio: the host smoke test uses 20 English and 20 Bulgarian utterances of the FLEURS test split (google/fleurs, CC BY 4.0, public read speech,
  no personal data); tools/voice/prepare_samples.py cuts them, they are never committed or shipped. Voice activity detection (Silero) is not used.

